# Keep the Docker build context small and, critically, keep real secrets
# out of image layers. Next.js standalone output copies an app's .env file
# straight into the image if it's present in the build context, so these
# MUST be excluded — runtime config is injected via docker-compose /
# platform env vars instead.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.next-e2e
**/.next-e2e-dev

.git
.github
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.md
!README.md

docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
